/-!
# The roots of unity may be assumed to lie in the base realization

The ladder of the descending `ℓ`-central series is climbed over a base realization: a smooth
surjection of the absolute Galois group of the rationals onto the finite group the split embedding
problem starts from.  Every arithmetic statement the rungs consume is a statement about the field
that realization cuts out, and the ones that are Kummer-theoretic want the roots of unity to be
there already.

They may be assumed to be.  The group the base realization names is arbitrary, so it may be
enlarged: adjoining a cyclotomic field to a finite Galois level of the realization gives a larger
finite Galois extension whose Galois group still covers the original group, and the split embedding
problem over the larger group has the original one as a quotient, the kernel being carried along
unchanged.  Solving the enlarged problem therefore solves the original, and the enlarged problem
comes with as many roots of unity in its base as were asked for.

The gain is recorded twice: as a level of the algebraic closure containing a prescribed group of
roots of unity and still covering the group one started from, and as a variant of the step of the
ladder which is only ever asked about base realizations whose fixed field contains those roots.

## Main definitions

* `Shafarevich.GenericLevelStepEPRoots` — **the step of the ladder, asked only of base realizations
  whose kernel fixes the roots of unity of order the square of the prime times the exponent of the
  kernel of the embedding problem.**

## Main results

* `InverseGalois.Shafarevich.exists_level_containing_roots` — a finite Galois level of the algebraic
  closure of the rationals which contains the roots of unity of a prescribed order and whose Galois
  group still covers the group one started from.
* `Shafarevich.genericLevelStepEPRoots_of_hasRungData` — the arithmetic package still buys the step
  when it is only supplied over such a base.
* `Shafarevich.splitPrimePowerEP_of_genericLevelStepEPRoots` — **and that restricted step still
  solves every split embedding problem with a kernel of prime power order.**

## Tags

Shafarevich's theorem, embedding problem, roots of unity, cyclotomic field, base realization
-/

namespace InverseGalois.Shafarevich

open InverseGalois.CFT

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000

/-! ### Enlarging the base realization by a cyclotomic field -/

/-- **A base realization may be replaced by one whose field contains prescribed roots of unity.**

A smooth surjection onto a finite group factors through a finite Galois level; adjoining the field
generated by a primitive `m`-th root of unity to that level enlarges it to a finite Galois extension
which contains every `m`-th root of unity, and the surjection, which kills the subgroup fixing the
smaller level, kills the smaller subgroup fixing the larger one and so factors through the Galois
group of the enlarged level. -/
theorem exists_level_containing_roots (U : Type) [Group U] [Finite U] [TopologicalSpace U]
    [DiscreteTopology U] (hU : IsInverseGalois U) (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] :
    ∃ (E : IntermediateField ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)) (_ : FiniteDimensional ℚ ↥E)
      (_ : IsGalois ℚ ↥E) (π : Gal(↥E/ℚ) →* U), Function.Surjective π ∧
        ∀ ζ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ, ζ ^ m = 1 → ζ ∈ E := by
  obtain ⟨φ₀, hsurj, hsm⟩ :=
    (isInverseGalois_iff_exists_smooth_surjective (Ω := AlgebraicClosure ℚ)).1 hU
  obtain ⟨E₀, hfin₀, hgal₀, ψ, hψ⟩ := exists_level_comp_restrictNormalHom_eq φ₀ hsm
  haveI := hfin₀
  haveI := hgal₀
  have hroots : ∀ ζ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ, ζ ^ m = 1 → ζ ∈ E₀ ⊔ cycSubfield m := by
    intro ζ hζ
    obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := (cycRoot_spec m).eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one hζ
    have hc : cycRoot m ∈ cycSubfield m := IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {cycRoot m} rfl
    have hp : cycRoot m ^ i ∈ cycSubfield m := pow_mem hc i
    exact (le_sup_right : cycSubfield m ≤ E₀ ⊔ cycSubfield m) hp
  have h2 : E₀.fixingSubgroup ≤ φ₀.ker := by
    intro σ hσ
    rw [← IntermediateField.restrictNormalHom_ker E₀] at hσ
    rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker, ← hψ σ, MonoidHom.mem_ker.1 hσ, _root_.map_one]
  have hker : (E₀ ⊔ cycSubfield m).fixingSubgroup ≤ φ₀.ker :=
    le_trans (IntermediateField.fixingSubgroup_le le_sup_left) h2
  obtain ⟨π, hπ⟩ := exists_monoidHom_comp_restrictNormalHom (E₀ ⊔ cycSubfield m) φ₀ hker
  refine ⟨E₀ ⊔ cycSubfield m, inferInstance, inferInstance, π, fun u => ?_, hroots⟩
  obtain ⟨σ, rfl⟩ := hsurj u
  exact ⟨AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom _ σ, hπ σ⟩

end InverseGalois.Shafarevich

namespace Shafarevich

open InverseGalois.CFT InverseGalois.Shafarevich

/-! ### The step of the ladder over a base with the roots of unity -/

/-- **One step of the ladder of the descending `ℓ`-central series, asked only over a base
realization whose field contains enough roots of unity.**

This is the step of the ladder with one hypothesis added to the base realization: the subgroup it
kills is required to fix every root of unity of order the square of the prime times the exponent of
the test group, which is to say that the field the realization cuts out contains them.  That is the
bound the ramification restriction is measured against, and it is uniform: a solution at any rung
and for any number of letters takes, at a prime where the base realization splits completely, only
values killed by the exponent of the test group.  Everything else — the family of subgroups and the
property chosen in advance, the bottom of the ladder asked for outright, and one rung following from
the previous one for every number of letters — is unchanged. -/
def GenericLevelStepEPRoots (ℓ : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (S U : Type) [Group S] [Finite S] [Group U] [Finite U] [TopologicalSpace U]
      [DiscreteTopology U] (Ω : Type) [Field Ω] [Algebra ℚ Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] [IsGalois ℚ Ω]
      (φ : Gal(Ω/ℚ) →* U), IsPGroup ℓ S → Function.Surjective φ → IsSmoothHom φ →
      (∀ x ∈ φ.ker, ∀ ζ : Ω, ζ ^ (ℓ * ℓ * Monoid.exponent S) = 1 → x ζ = ζ) →
    ∃ (T : Set (Subgroup Gal(Ω/ℚ))) (P : LevelProperty ℓ U S ℚ Ω),
      (∀ i : ℕ, LevelSolution ℓ U S φ T P i 0) ∧ ∀ j : ℕ,
        (∀ i : ℕ, LevelSolution ℓ U S φ T P i j) → ∀ n : ℕ, LevelSolution ℓ U S φ T P n (j + 1)

/-- **The arithmetic package buys the restricted step of the ladder just as it buys the
unrestricted one**, the extra hypothesis on the base realization being carried straight through to
the place where the package is supplied. -/
theorem genericLevelStepEPRoots_of_hasRungData (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime]
    (h : ∀ (S U : Type) [Group S] [Finite S] [Group U] [Finite U] [TopologicalSpace U]
        [DiscreteTopology U] (Ω : Type) [Field Ω] [Algebra ℚ Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] [IsGalois ℚ Ω]
        (φ : Gal(Ω/ℚ) →* U), IsPGroup ℓ S → Function.Surjective φ → IsSmoothHom φ →
        (∀ x ∈ φ.ker, ∀ ζ : Ω, ζ ^ (ℓ * ℓ * Monoid.exponent S) = 1 → x ζ = ζ) →
      ∃ (t : ℕ) (D : Fin t → Subgroup Gal(Ω/ℚ)) (T : Set (Subgroup Gal(Ω/ℚ)))
          (P : LevelProperty ℓ U S ℚ Ω), HasRungData ℓ U S φ D T P) :
    GenericLevelStepEPRoots ℓ := by
  intro S U _ _ _ _ _ _ Ω _ _ _ _ φ hS hsurj hsm hroots
  obtain ⟨t, D, T, P, hdata⟩ := h S U Ω φ hS hsurj hsm hroots
  exact ⟨Set.range D, P, hdata.1,
    fun j hj n => levelSolution_succ_of_hasRungData ℓ U S hS φ D T P hdata j hj n⟩

/-! ### The reduction -/

/-- **A cyclotomic level solves the generic split embedding problem over its own Galois group.**
The Galois group of a finite Galois extension containing the roots of unity of order the square of
the prime times the exponent of the kernel is realized by restriction from the algebraic closure,
and the subgroup that restriction kills fixes the extension and hence those roots of unity, so the
restricted step of the ladder applies to it. -/
theorem isInverseGalois_generic_of_genericLevelStepEPRoots {ℓ : ℕ} [Fact ℓ.Prime]
    (h : GenericLevelStepEPRoots ℓ) (S : Type) [Group S] [Finite S] (hS : IsPGroup ℓ S) (n : ℕ)
    (E : IntermediateField ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)) [FiniteDimensional ℚ ↥E] [IsGalois ℚ ↥E]
    (hroots : ∀ ζ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ, ζ ^ (ℓ * ℓ * Monoid.exponent S) = 1 → ζ ∈ E) :
    IsInverseGalois (Generic Gal(↥E/ℚ) n S ⋊[genericAut Gal(↥E/ℚ) n S] Gal(↥E/ℚ)) := by
  letI : TopologicalSpace Gal(↥E/ℚ) := ⊥
  haveI : DiscreteTopology Gal(↥E/ℚ) := ⟨rfl⟩
  have hker : ∀ x ∈ (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom (F := ℚ) (K₁ := AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥E).ker,
      ∀ ζ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ, ζ ^ (ℓ * ℓ * Monoid.exponent S) = 1 → x ζ = ζ := by
    intro x hx ζ hζ
    rw [IntermediateField.restrictNormalHom_ker] at hx
    simp only [IntermediateField.mem_fixingSubgroup_iff] at hx
    exact hx ζ (hroots ζ hζ)
  obtain ⟨T, P, hbase, hstep⟩ :=
    h S Gal(↥E/ℚ) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)
      (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom (F := ℚ) (K₁ := AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥E) hS
      (restrictNormalHom_surjective_level E)
      (isSmoothHom_of_isOpenNormal_ker (isOpenNormal_ker_restrictNormalHom E)) hker
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := exists_pCentral_eq_bot ℓ (isPGroup_generic Gal(↥E/ℚ) n S hS)
  exact isInverseGalois_of_levelSolution Gal(↥E/ℚ) S hj
    (forall_levelSolution Gal(↥E/ℚ) S hbase hstep j n)

/-- **The restricted step of the ladder still solves every split embedding problem with a kernel of
prime power order.**

Given such a problem, the group it is posed over is covered by the Galois group of a finite Galois
extension containing the roots of unity of the prescribed order, and the same kernel with the action
pulled back along that covering poses a problem over the larger group.  The restricted step solves
the generic problem there, hence the pulled back one, and the original problem is its quotient by a
map which is the identity on the kernel and the covering on the outer factor. -/
theorem splitPrimePowerEP_of_genericLevelStepEPRoots
    (h : ∀ ℓ : ℕ, ℓ.Prime → GenericLevelStepEPRoots ℓ) : SplitPrimePowerEP := by
  intro H U _ _ _ _ p hp hH φ hU
  haveI : NeZero (p * p * Monoid.exponent H) :=
    ⟨mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero hp.out.ne_zero hp.out.ne_zero) Monoid.exponent_ne_zero_of_finite⟩
  letI : TopologicalSpace U := ⊥
  haveI : DiscreteTopology U := ⟨rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨E, hfin, hgal, π, hπsurj, hroots⟩ :=
    exists_level_containing_roots U hU (p * p * Monoid.exponent H)
  haveI := hfin
  haveI := hgal
  have hgen : IsInverseGalois (H ⋊[φ.comp π] Gal(↥E/ℚ)) :=
    isInverseGalois_semidirectProduct_of_generic (φ.comp π)
      (isInverseGalois_generic_of_genericLevelStepEPRoots (h p hp.out) H hH (Nat.card H) E hroots)
  refine hgen.of_surjective (SemidirectProduct.map (MonoidHom.id H) π fun g => rfl) ?_
  rintro ⟨x, u⟩
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := hπsurj u
  exact ⟨⟨x, g⟩, by ext <;> simp⟩

end Shafarevich
